WEBVTT

00:01.890 --> 00:05.026
♪ It seems today
that all you see ♪

00:05.093 --> 00:08.362
♪ Is violence in movies
and sex on TV ♪

00:08.430 --> 00:11.515
♪ But where are those
good old-fashioned values ♪

00:11.567 --> 00:14.468
♪ On which we used to rely? ♪

00:14.536 --> 00:18.406
♪ Lucky there's a family guy ♪

00:18.490 --> 00:21.242
♪ Lucky there's a man
who positively can do ♪

00:21.326 --> 00:22.860
♪ All the things that make us ♪

00:22.928 --> 00:24.211
♪ Laugh and cry ♪

00:24.296 --> 00:28.967
♪ He's... a...
Fam... ily... Guy! ♪

00:34.409 --> 00:35.976
TV ANNOUNCER:
And now back to

00:36.044 --> 00:37.912
the Disney Channel's
exclusive presentation,

00:37.979 --> 00:40.814
<i>Aladdin 5:
Jafar Answers the Census.</i>

00:40.882 --> 00:43.517
Okay, and how many people
live in your palace?

00:43.585 --> 00:45.486
Um, does the bird count?

00:45.554 --> 00:47.321
Does the bird live here?

00:47.389 --> 00:49.557
Yes.
Then, yes, the bird counts.

00:49.624 --> 00:51.091
Uh, okay. Two.

00:51.159 --> 00:52.526
Great.

00:52.594 --> 00:54.428
What is your primary
source of income?

00:54.496 --> 00:56.730
Um, sorcery.

00:56.798 --> 00:58.766
And a little
from political corruption,

00:58.833 --> 01:00.501
but primarily sorcery.

01:00.569 --> 01:02.570
Yeah, I'll just
put sorcery.

01:02.637 --> 01:06.106
Okay. Um, are you gay,
straight or not sure?

01:06.174 --> 01:08.309
Uh, why are you
asking me this?

01:08.376 --> 01:10.945
It's just... I-I don't...
I don't write the questions.

01:11.012 --> 01:13.180
I know. It just seems a little personal.
Yeah, I-I understand.

01:13.248 --> 01:14.515
You're... you're free
not to answer it

01:14.583 --> 01:15.749
if that's your choice.

01:15.817 --> 01:17.885
No, no, no, it's okay.
You can put "not sure."

01:17.953 --> 01:20.120
All right.
I'm off to Paris.

01:20.188 --> 01:22.439
You guys going to be okay
without me for a week?

01:22.507 --> 01:23.874
Ugh. I don't know.

01:23.925 --> 01:25.726
I mean, who's going to put
those three magazines

01:25.794 --> 01:27.511
in a neat stack
on the coffee table?

01:27.562 --> 01:29.163
Lois, I realize you're excited
about going away

01:29.230 --> 01:31.231
with Bonnie and all,
but could I... could I not

01:31.299 --> 01:33.267
have to hear about the trip
when you get back?

01:33.335 --> 01:34.802
I-I just...
I know you're going to have

01:34.869 --> 01:36.370
pictures and stories,
and I-I just...

01:36.438 --> 01:38.689
I-I-I just don't want to be
involved in any of that mess.

01:38.740 --> 01:39.940
(knock at door)

01:41.326 --> 01:42.710
You ready to go, Lois?

01:42.777 --> 01:44.428
I sure am.
Oh, my God, Bonnie.

01:44.496 --> 01:46.130
We're going to have
such a good time.

01:46.197 --> 01:49.083
I know, and it's going to be
so much fun going with you.

01:49.150 --> 01:50.584
Joe hates to fly

01:50.669 --> 01:52.920
'cause they always put him
underneath with the dogs.

01:52.988 --> 01:54.471
(dogs barking)

01:54.539 --> 01:57.107
Indonesia better be worth it.

01:57.175 --> 01:58.842
Okay. Bye, everyone.

01:58.910 --> 02:00.844
Kids, you mind your father
while I'm gone.

02:00.912 --> 02:02.046
Love you.

02:02.097 --> 02:03.347
Bye, Mom.
Bye!

02:03.414 --> 02:04.598
Oh, Peter,
I almost forgot.

02:04.666 --> 02:05.883
Here's some money
for groceries

02:05.934 --> 02:07.601
and a list
of the kids' schedules.

02:07.669 --> 02:09.236
The fat man in charge
for a week?

02:09.304 --> 02:11.005
He's going to be in
over his head.

02:11.072 --> 02:12.873
Like when he was a boxing coach.

02:12.941 --> 02:14.308
Punch him! Punch him again!
Punch him!

02:14.392 --> 02:15.926
Punch him now! Again!
Now you're getting punched!

02:15.977 --> 02:17.394
Punch back!
Don't let him hit you!

02:17.445 --> 02:19.096
Get out of the way!
Punch him!

02:19.147 --> 02:21.048
(bell clangs)
You know what I'm going to tell you.

02:21.116 --> 02:22.983
I got to punch him...
You got to punch him more.

02:27.055 --> 02:28.839
Hey, you ever check
Joe's Facebook?

02:28.907 --> 02:30.691
Ugh, I know. Awful.

02:30.759 --> 02:33.994
"Hittin' Cheesecake
Factory again. So amped."

02:34.062 --> 02:35.996
And then the symbol
that means "wink."

02:36.064 --> 02:37.998
Really? I mean, like,
why... why the wink?

02:38.066 --> 02:39.433
I mean, is there...
is there something

02:39.501 --> 02:40.834
that we're supposed
to be in on?

02:40.902 --> 02:42.569
Is he not going there?

02:42.637 --> 02:44.438
Is he... is
he not amped?

02:44.506 --> 02:46.707
And-and... and who cares
if he is, you know?

02:46.775 --> 02:48.275
Dick.

02:48.343 --> 02:51.645
Coming up, our horribly outdated
scams reporter, Ken Redowski,

02:51.713 --> 02:53.714
gets angry about a product
you don't care about.

02:53.782 --> 02:55.516
Digital bathroom scales!

02:55.583 --> 02:56.884
Thanks, Ken.
This just in:

02:56.951 --> 02:58.952
there has been a confirmed
outbreak of goat flu

02:59.020 --> 03:00.454
at James Woods High School.

03:00.522 --> 03:02.072
Goat flu?
You got to be kidding me.

03:02.140 --> 03:03.374
Every year, the stupid media

03:03.441 --> 03:05.192
tries to scare us
with this kind of thing,

03:05.260 --> 03:07.077
and every year,
it turns out to be nothing.

03:07.145 --> 03:08.562
Yeah, it's nothing.
I know.

03:08.630 --> 03:10.080
Every year, it's nothing.
Well, now, hang on.

03:10.148 --> 03:11.315
There might be
something to this.

03:11.383 --> 03:12.483
Health officials have said

03:12.550 --> 03:14.351
that a vaccine
is not yet available.

03:14.419 --> 03:16.186
And if you're not scared yet,
here's some footage

03:16.254 --> 03:18.188
of people sneezing
at a salad bar.

03:18.256 --> 03:20.991
(sneezing)

03:21.059 --> 03:22.826
Oh, dear.
Here's some footage

03:22.894 --> 03:24.428
of people licking
subway turnstiles.

03:27.132 --> 03:29.133
Oh.
Here's some footage of a man

03:29.200 --> 03:31.168
with the flu making out with you
while you're asleep.

03:34.139 --> 03:35.339
Oh, my God!

03:35.407 --> 03:36.740
While James Woods High
remains open,

03:36.808 --> 03:39.209
students are reminded
to wash their hands frequently

03:39.277 --> 03:41.245
and watch for early signs
of infection.

03:41.312 --> 03:43.547
Oh, my God. I got to get
the kids out of there.

03:43.615 --> 03:44.815
What?
What are you talking about?

03:44.866 --> 03:46.133
I'm talking
about homeschooling, Brian.

03:46.201 --> 03:48.068
Just until the crisis is over.

03:48.136 --> 03:49.236
Peter, that's a complete
overreaction.

03:49.304 --> 03:50.637
I don't think
Lois would be happy

03:50.705 --> 03:52.355
if you pulled the kids
out of school.

03:52.407 --> 03:53.891
Well, she left me in charge,
didn't she?

03:53.958 --> 03:55.392
And besides, you know me.

03:55.460 --> 03:58.011
When I set my mind to something,
I am not easily deterred.

03:58.079 --> 04:00.013
Like when I tried out
to be an Olympic gymnast.

04:01.449 --> 04:02.833
(inhales deeply)

04:04.085 --> 04:05.535
(gun fires)

04:07.155 --> 04:08.439
You did it, Peter.

04:08.506 --> 04:09.807
Why'd you shoot me?

04:09.874 --> 04:11.575
Because I'm weird,
creepy coach.

04:11.643 --> 04:14.244
Now, let me give you
inappropriate personal shower

04:14.312 --> 04:17.247
while I smoke and forbid
you to see parent.

04:17.315 --> 04:20.017
This is... Somebody should
look into this sport.

04:24.389 --> 04:26.457
Uh, I'd like to apologize
for yesterday,

04:26.524 --> 04:28.192
when I assigned you
lab partners.

04:28.259 --> 04:30.894
It has come to my attention
that this is an English class.

04:30.962 --> 04:32.329
(knock at door)

04:33.448 --> 04:34.481
(indistinct whispering)

04:34.549 --> 04:35.616
Griffin?

04:39.521 --> 04:42.022
Chris, Meg, I spoke to
your father on the phone,

04:42.090 --> 04:44.191
and he said you needed to
be removed from school.

04:44.259 --> 04:46.293
I didn't believe it was
really him at first,

04:46.361 --> 04:47.594
but then I received
another call

04:47.662 --> 04:49.363
from the very person
who I thought

04:49.430 --> 04:51.064
was pretending
to be him.

04:51.132 --> 04:52.966
It caused quite a
stir in my office.

04:59.057 --> 05:00.090
Come on, children.

05:02.694 --> 05:03.961
Is everything
all right?

05:04.028 --> 05:04.962
Everything's fine.

05:05.029 --> 05:06.363
It's me.

05:06.431 --> 05:08.532
I just dressed up like your
father to jazz your teachers

05:08.600 --> 05:09.500
and get you
out of here.

05:09.567 --> 05:10.534
What do you mean?

05:10.602 --> 05:11.602
I'm taking you
out of here.

05:11.669 --> 05:13.136
That place is riddled
with goat flu,

05:13.204 --> 05:14.555
so I'm gonna homeschool
you kids.

05:14.622 --> 05:15.622
Oh, okay.

05:15.690 --> 05:17.124
Dad, where'd you
get this car?

05:17.192 --> 05:18.559
I borrowed it
from Quagmire.

05:18.626 --> 05:21.445
He's not home 'cause he got
abducted by aliens last night.

05:21.513 --> 05:24.047
So, do you guys just not do
the anal probe anymore?

05:24.115 --> 05:26.250
Is that...?
No, that's more or less been retired.

05:26.317 --> 05:28.452
I see, I see.

05:28.520 --> 05:30.420
D-Do you still have the thing?

05:33.691 --> 05:36.877
Oh, my God,
what a beautiful room.

05:36.945 --> 05:38.712
Paris is so incredible.

05:38.780 --> 05:40.480
I can't believe
we're really here.

05:40.548 --> 05:41.882
I know.

05:41.950 --> 05:45.452
Look at all the
people on the street.

05:45.520 --> 05:47.120
Not a lot of people
of color here,

05:47.188 --> 05:49.323
but the ones that are
black are really black.

05:49.390 --> 05:51.091
I've noticed that, too.

05:51.159 --> 05:52.993
All right, I've got
our whole day planned.

05:53.061 --> 05:54.394
First, we'll go
to the Louvre.

05:54.462 --> 05:57.064
Then we'll go shopping
along the Champs-Elys├йes.

05:57.131 --> 05:59.333
Uh, Lois, I should
probably tell you

05:59.400 --> 06:02.836
I didn't come all the way here
to go to museums and shops.

06:02.904 --> 06:04.404
Well, I-I don't understand.

06:04.472 --> 06:06.506
Why'd you even want
to come here, then?

06:06.574 --> 06:09.676
Lois, I came here
to have an affair.

06:09.744 --> 06:10.844
An affair?

06:10.912 --> 06:12.012
With who?

06:12.080 --> 06:14.381
Anyone.
My God.

06:14.449 --> 06:15.649
Well, can we
at least do

06:15.717 --> 06:18.285
some Muppet-style
sightseeing first?

06:18.353 --> 06:20.187
(accordion music playing)

06:40.636 --> 06:42.204
All right, settle down.

06:42.253 --> 06:43.336
Good morning, class.

06:43.404 --> 06:44.704
BOTH:
Morning, Dad.

06:44.789 --> 06:46.506
We're going to need a few
things for this class--

06:46.591 --> 06:48.875
an eagerness to learn,
a thirst for knowledge--

06:48.943 --> 06:51.778
but one thing we
won't need is this.

06:51.846 --> 06:53.647
That's right, I know
you're all used to teachers

06:53.714 --> 06:57.133
wearing tuxedos and Dracula
capes, but not this one.

06:57.185 --> 06:59.519
There will be no pretense
in this classroom.

06:59.604 --> 07:02.889
There will only be open
minds and new horizons.

07:02.957 --> 07:05.609
Get ready for adventure.

07:05.676 --> 07:07.544
I know some teachers
think class should be

07:07.612 --> 07:11.164
an exercise in structure,
but not Mr. Griffin.

07:11.232 --> 07:13.400
This is what my
class will be, this!

07:13.484 --> 07:14.367
Learn with me!

07:14.452 --> 07:15.368
Let's teach each other!

07:15.453 --> 07:17.320
Yay, learning!

07:19.457 --> 07:21.524
Chris, "A."

07:21.576 --> 07:23.410
Meg, "F."

07:27.865 --> 07:30.967
Ah, you know, this is
how you take a vacation.

07:31.035 --> 07:32.736
Oh, Bonnie, would
you look at that?

07:32.803 --> 07:35.071
I've never seen anything
like that before--

07:35.139 --> 07:37.507
a croissant with
almonds on it.

07:37.575 --> 07:39.309
And, and could you
bring me a beer?

07:39.376 --> 07:41.411
Oh, I feel
so elegant.

07:41.479 --> 07:42.412
What are you
going to have?

07:42.480 --> 07:43.914
You know
what I'd really like?

07:43.981 --> 07:46.550
A piece of that.

07:46.617 --> 07:48.285
Bonnie, for God's
sake, stop it.

07:48.352 --> 07:51.922
Lois, I already told you, I'm
in Paris to have an affair.

07:51.989 --> 07:54.391
I'll even do a Muslim
if I have to.

07:54.458 --> 07:56.092
But I just can't believe
you'd throw away

07:56.160 --> 07:59.296
all those years with Joe just
to have some silly fling.

07:59.363 --> 08:01.698
I'm not throwing
anything away.

08:01.766 --> 08:04.801
Joe and I have been growing
apart for a long time.

08:04.869 --> 08:06.503
Besides, we've had
a good run.

08:06.571 --> 08:08.471
We've been married
for 80 years.

08:08.539 --> 08:09.806
You what?

08:09.874 --> 08:12.342
Well, that's in married-
to-a-handicapped-guy years.

08:12.410 --> 08:13.977
Go, Dallas Cowboys, huh?

08:14.045 --> 08:15.011
Hello.

08:15.079 --> 08:16.146
Excuse me?

08:16.213 --> 08:17.948
You are American, no?

08:18.015 --> 08:20.750
I very much admire
your Garry Shandling.

08:20.801 --> 08:22.435
Look, I know where
you're going with this,

08:22.503 --> 08:23.637
and we're not
interested, okay,

08:23.721 --> 08:25.255
so you might as well
just keep moving.

08:25.323 --> 08:26.256
I'm interested.

08:26.324 --> 08:28.658
(laughing lasciviously)

08:28.726 --> 08:29.993
Bonnie.

08:30.061 --> 08:32.495
Would you like to sample
a warm French baguette?

08:32.563 --> 08:33.830
Oh, my.

08:33.898 --> 08:36.399
My intention is to
void myself on you.

08:36.467 --> 08:39.869
Oh, I'd almost forgotten
what it's like to be romanced.

08:39.937 --> 08:41.204
Come on, Bonnie,
we are leaving.

08:41.272 --> 08:42.272
What?

08:42.340 --> 08:44.257
Look, I'm doing
you a favor.

08:44.325 --> 08:47.193
My stool will sleep
alone tonight.

08:48.913 --> 08:51.064
Bonnie, this is insanity.

08:51.132 --> 08:52.599
Promise me you'll put
this whole affair thing

08:52.667 --> 08:53.700
out of your head.

08:53.768 --> 08:55.769
Lois, I'm just
having fun.

08:55.836 --> 08:57.337
You're playing
with fire.

08:57.405 --> 08:59.105
Look, no marriage
is perfect,

08:59.173 --> 09:01.625
but Joe's the man you
gave your life to,

09:01.692 --> 09:03.877
and besides, you
have a little girl.

09:03.945 --> 09:06.379
You really want to be setting
this kind of example?

09:06.447 --> 09:07.580
(sighs)

09:07.648 --> 09:09.249
I guess you're right, Lois.

09:09.317 --> 09:10.850
It's just that sometimes I feel

09:10.918 --> 09:13.219
like I don't even know
Joe anymore.

09:13.287 --> 09:17.240
It's like I've become a
different person and so has he.

09:17.307 --> 09:19.909
<i>(American Dad theme playing)</i>

09:19.977 --> 09:22.746
♪ Good morning, USA! ♪

09:22.813 --> 09:26.583
♪ I got a feeling that it's
gonna be a wonderful day ♪

09:26.650 --> 09:29.519
♪ The sun in the sky
has a smile on his face ♪

09:29.587 --> 09:33.056
♪ And he's shining a salute
to the American race ♪

09:35.843 --> 09:38.995
♪ Oh, boy, it's swell to say ♪

09:39.046 --> 09:42.799
♪ Good morning, USA ♪

09:44.168 --> 09:47.053
<i>♪ Good morning, USA! ♪</i>

09:48.556 --> 09:50.223
All right, class, this
course is going to cover

09:50.291 --> 09:52.542
all the significant
moments in human history,

09:52.610 --> 09:54.461
starting with the settling
of the Old West,

09:54.528 --> 09:57.614
where brave pioneers survived
against long odds.

09:59.433 --> 10:01.851
Honey, I have to go into town
to get some supplies,

10:01.902 --> 10:04.504
so I'm probably going to die,
but if I don't,

10:04.572 --> 10:07.040
I'll see you in 18 months
with a canvas bag of salt

10:07.108 --> 10:09.209
and a tin of whale fat
for the children.

10:09.276 --> 10:11.111
I've dug graves out back
for all of you

10:11.178 --> 10:13.413
in the likely event that you,
too, shall perish.

10:13.481 --> 10:15.348
WOMAN:
You were a good man, Abraham.

10:15.416 --> 10:17.117
Please scrawl that
on a rough-hewn piece of wood

10:17.184 --> 10:18.118
in my honor.

10:18.185 --> 10:20.053
I shall.

10:22.807 --> 10:24.858
The reign of Henry VIII.

10:24.925 --> 10:27.227
Did you enjoy what I
just did for you, sire?

10:27.294 --> 10:28.862
Yes, very much so.

10:28.929 --> 10:32.165
Wow, when this is over, I am
definitely keeping her head.

10:32.233 --> 10:34.768
Joseph Smith discovering
the Book of Mormon.

10:34.852 --> 10:37.704
Oh, an old
Con Ed bill--

10:37.772 --> 10:39.489
I mean, a new testament
of Jesus Christ;

10:39.556 --> 10:40.740
everyone has
to sleep with me.

10:40.825 --> 10:42.459
What?
And no dancing.

10:42.526 --> 10:44.227
But recent years have also seen

10:44.295 --> 10:46.346
many important
historical events.

10:46.414 --> 10:50.483
1985 brought us the gayest
music video of all time.

10:50.551 --> 10:53.870
(echoing whistle)

10:53.921 --> 10:57.457
Okay, Tokyo.

10:57.541 --> 11:01.127
South America,
Australia, France.

11:01.212 --> 11:02.929
Germany, U.K.

11:02.997 --> 11:06.415
(whistling)
Africa!

11:06.467 --> 11:09.018
(upbeat intro to "Dancing in
the Street" featuring trumpets)

11:13.858 --> 11:17.310
♪ Calling out
around the world ♪

11:17.394 --> 11:21.064
♪ Are you ready
for a brand-new beat? ♪

11:21.115 --> 11:24.284
♪ Summer's here,
and the time is right ♪

11:24.368 --> 11:27.070
♪ For dancing in the street ♪

11:27.121 --> 11:29.605
♪ Dancing in Chicago ♪

11:29.657 --> 11:31.040
<i>♪ Dancing in the street ♪</i>

11:31.108 --> 11:32.909
♪ Down in New Orleans ♪

11:32.960 --> 11:34.277
<i>♪ Dancing in the street ♪</i>

11:34.328 --> 11:36.129
♪ In New York City ♪

11:36.213 --> 11:37.413
<i>♪ Dancing in the street ♪</i>

11:37.465 --> 11:40.834
♪ All we need is music,
sweet music ♪

11:40.918 --> 11:42.669
<i>♪ Sweet music ♪</i>

11:42.753 --> 11:44.453
♪ There'll be music
everywhere ♪

11:44.505 --> 11:45.889
<i>♪ Everywhere ♪</i>

11:45.956 --> 11:50.143
♪ They'll be swinging, swaying,
records playing ♪

11:50.227 --> 11:52.846
♪ Dancing in the street ♪

11:52.930 --> 11:55.014
♪ Whoa ♪

11:55.099 --> 11:57.183
♪ It doesn't matter
what you wear ♪

11:57.268 --> 12:00.303
♪ Just as long
as you are there ♪

12:00.354 --> 12:04.607
♪ So come on, every guy,
grab a girl ♪

12:04.658 --> 12:08.077
♪ Everywhere
around the world ♪

12:08.145 --> 12:10.697
♪ They'll be dancing ♪

12:10.781 --> 12:12.832
♪ Dancing in the street ♪

12:12.917 --> 12:15.335
<i>♪ Dancing in the street ♪</i>

12:15.419 --> 12:19.539
♪ It's an invitation
across the nation ♪

12:19.623 --> 12:23.259
♪ A chance for folks to meet ♪

12:23.327 --> 12:25.178
♪ They'll be laughing
and singing ♪

12:25.262 --> 12:26.713
♪ And music swinging ♪

12:26.797 --> 12:29.215
♪ Dancing in the street ♪

12:29.300 --> 12:31.217
♪ Philadelphia, PA ♪

12:31.302 --> 12:32.886
<i>♪ Dancing in the street ♪</i>

12:32.970 --> 12:34.938
♪ Baltimore in DC now ♪

12:35.005 --> 12:36.639
